[{:adr/consequences ["Any actor can today commit 80-data/public/*.journal.edn and get\n   git-clone-readable public data immediately -- but without the (not yet\n   built) ingestion job, it stays 'git-readable, not yet kotobase-queryable'.\n   Closing that gap is the concrete next implementation step this ADR\n   defines the shape for." "Gives ADR-2607032430's D2 convergence target ('actor = shard = repo = RID\n   = graph = IPNS head') the concrete file-placement/schema decision it was\n   missing." "Reframes kotobase.net from sole store to derived index over a\n   git-authoritative source -- a scope shift relevant to ADR-2607051410's\n   future distributed-storage-mesh work; recorded here as a cross-reference,\n   not a rewrite of that ADR." "DataLad's scope stays large-binary-only/opt-in, explicitly NOT extended\n   to general public-data replication in this ADR -- any future proposal to\n   widen it should account for this decision."], :adr/authoritative_for ["An actor repo's own git history (a committed EDN quad-log under\n    80-data/public/*.journal.edn) is the authoritative source of an actor's\n    PUBLIC data -- not kotobase.net" "kotobase.net/kotobase-peer is a derived, rebuildable read index over\n    that git-resident journal, not the sole store, for any actor that\n    adopts this pattern" "DataLad (git-annex + B2) remains scoped to large-binary payloads a\n    journal references by CID, extending the existing m365-archive/\n    mangaka-data pattern per-actor on an opt-in basis -- not a general\n    replication layer for structured public data" "kotoba-rad's role is unchanged from ADR-2607072200 (identity/\n    authorization only): it signs and gates the journal's commits/refs once\n    an actor repo runs on real kotoba-git history, but this ADR does not\n    expand kotoba-rad into a data store"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "actor-public-data-git-journal-kotobase-index", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607072200-kotoba-git-kotoba-rad-content-addressed-vcs.md" "90-docs/adr/2607032430-kotoba-datom-log-structured-engine-redesign.md" "90-docs/adr/2607022300-itonami-gftdcojp-private-tenant-kotoba-rad-git-storage.md" "90-docs/adr/2607051410-net-kotobase-distributed-storage-mesh-design.md" "90-docs/adr/2606282000-cloud-workers-kotobase-external-storage.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2606231200-kotoba-rad-sovereign-actor-identity.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2606251200-kotoba-rad-git-transport-binding.md"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607072300-actor-public-data-git-journal-kotobase-index", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-07", :adr/decision "{:summary \"An actor's public data is authored as an EDN quad-log\\n            (80-data/public/*.journal.edn) committed directly into the\\n            actor's own repo -- the source of truth. kotobase.net/\\n            kotobase-peer becomes a derived, rebuildable index folded from\\n            that journal. DataLad stays scoped to large binaries the\\n            journal references by CID. kotoba-rad's role is unchanged from\\n            ADR-2607072200.\", :layering [\"actor repo (GitHub, same transport as today) ->\\n    80-data/public/*.journal.edn: source of truth, EDN-reader-readable via\\n    plain git clone/west update, no server required\" \"Tier 1 (usable today, no new infra): journal file format identical to\\n    the existing identity journal's EDN quad vectors\\n    [\\\"<subject-cid-or-id>\\\" :attr value tx :add]; GitHub remains transport;\\n    does not wait for kotoba-git/kotoba-rad production wiring\" \"Tier 2 (future, after ADR-2607072200's own flagged transport/p2p\\n    follow-up lands): once an actor repo's canonical VCS host is kotoba-git\\n    itself, kotoba-git.repo/persist!'s arrangement quads ARE this journal;\\n    the flat EDN file becomes a derived artifact, not the source; kotoba-rad\\n    sigref/push-gate applies unchanged (it only ever handles plain CID\\n    strings) -- no new kotoba-rad code needed\" \"kotobase-peer ingestion (fold job, NOT implemented in this ADR): reads\\n    the journal and folds it into arrangement, so kotobase.net's XRPC\\n    graph.query surface (already assumed by actor-manifest.jsonld) serves\\n    low-latency indexed queries -- but the index is rebuildable from the\\n    journal, reversing today's 'kotobase.net is the only store' posture,\\n    and providing one mitigation to the single-point-of-failure posture\\n    flagged in ADR-2607051410\" \"DataLad (git-annex + B2, opt-in per-actor): only for large binaries a\\n    journal references by CID (images/video/model weights); journal stores\\n    the CID reference only, never the bytes -- mirrors kotoba-git's own\\n    'log holds content hash, bytes live elsewhere' shape; registered in\\n    manifest/repos.edn :datalad exactly like m365-archive/mangaka-data\" \"kotoba-rad role unchanged from ADR-2607072200: identity/authorization\\n    only, no data-store or replication responsibilities added\"], :not-decided [\"No ingestion pipeline (journal -> kotobase-peer fold job) code written\\n    here -- trigger mechanism (west update hook, GitHub webhook, kotobase.net\\n    pull) left undecided, design only.\" \"No migration of the existing 320 identity journals, nor of any actor's\\n    existing kotobase business data, into this 80-data/public/ format --\\n    same 'follow-up, not done here' status ADR-2607072200 already gave this\\n    class of migration.\" \"No pilot actor selected -- which actor first adopts\\n    80-data/public/*.journal.edn is an implementation-time decision.\" \"No new conflict-resolution/merge convention for concurrent journal\\n    commits across parallel agent sessions -- relies on CLAUDE.md's existing\\n    worktree-per-agent + server-side-merge conventions, not re-derived here.\" \"kotoba-git/kotoba-rad's own not-wired-to-production status is unchanged\\n    -- Tier 2 still waits on ADR-2607072200's own flagged p2p/transport\\n    patch; this ADR does not pull that forward.\" \"No per-domain attribute vocabulary (e.g. :cargo/*, :gtin/*) decided for\\n    80-data/public/ journals -- left to each actor's own implementation.\"]}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"Session question: for etzhayyim (and similar) actors, is there a\\n           design where PUBLIC data lives in the git repo itself, DataLad\\n           replicates large data, Radicle plays some role, and kotobase can\\n           query it? Owner instruction after research: \\\"do it\\\" (write the\\n           unifying ADR).\", :facts [\"Actor git repos (e.g. orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-cargo) hold only\\n    actor-manifest.jsonld (config incl. graph.query step DEFINITIONS) and\\n    .well-known/did.json -- zero literal business-data files committed.\" \"An actor's actual data (\\\"the graph\\\") lives only in kotobase-peer/\\n    kotobase.net, reachable only via transact/q/pull/datoms XRPC -- git\\n    clone/west update + file read cannot reach it.\" \"kotoba-rad (ADR-2607072200) is RID/delegate/sigref/push-gate only; no\\n    replication/gossip (kotoba-rad/README.md, explicit).\" \"DataLad (manifest/repos.edn :datalad) covers exactly two datasets --\\n    m365-archive, mangaka-data -- both large-binary archives, unrelated to\\n    actor public data.\" \"The only git-resident, server-free public data today is\\n    orgs/etzhayyim/root/80-data/kotoba-rad/*.identity.journal.edn (320\\n    files, EDN quad-log [cid attr value tx op], verified on disk) -- but\\n    scoped to identity facts only, not business data.\" \"ADR-2607032430 (D2) already targets 'actor = shard = repo = RID = graph\\n    = IPNS head' convergence; ADR-2607072200 already built the kotoba-git/\\n    kotoba-rad primitives on kotobase-peer -- but neither decided WHERE/HOW\\n    an actor's actual public data should be placed to realize that\\n    convergence.\"]}", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/verification ["Zero implementation (design only). Grounded in on-disk verification of\n   the existing identity journal file format, kotobase-peer's\n   transact/q/pull API shape, and manifest/repos.edn's :datalad section\n   format -- but no actor has written an 80-data/public/*.journal.edn file\n   yet, and no ingestion job exists."], :adr/title "ADR-2607072300: actor public data git-repo residency -- git journal as source of truth, kotobase.net as derived index, DataLad opt-in for large binaries only"}]